#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133828 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133643 :question/id #uuid "25d6bb34-eeb6-5bb7-8b66-0e6424244eeb" :question/math-academy-id "e-6285" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r\n$$ given that $\\mathbf F(x, y) = y \\,\\mathbf i + (x+y)\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf r(t) = (1+2t)\\,\\mathbf{i} + (1-t)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t \\in [0, 1].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r  = \\int_a^b\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r (t))\\cdot \\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx = 1 + 2t, \\qquad y = 1 - t .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(x+y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(1-t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+((1+2t)+(1-t))\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(1-t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(t+2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =((1-t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(t+2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =(1-t)\\cdot 2+(t+2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2-2t-t-2 \\\\  & =-3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-3t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16a9183a-68b4-5bad-b2d8-3bcf6597f263" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712402 :question-generator/id #uuid "8ccda1bb-2144-5d59-bb2a-d7b49c6e6cc1" :question-generator/script "generators/f3/f30db06b5fe742b1d3565d39b8c249abd0a361cce5be5f160afdeebefce19b20/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35328e91-1ef1-5761-9a3c-7f67ec2a2ca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257250} {:answer/id #uuid "3b66565f-5714-54a9-85c4-0ff27d7118fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257312} {:answer/id #uuid "5c0c7184-545c-5854-8b44-bd9cc2b4d287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257584} {:answer/id #uuid "682aa2b5-99c5-55c1-864f-3d951936c921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257703} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e0611e-d7f4-59c9-b753-ef6a1ce7a6dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35328e91-1ef1-5761-9a3c-7f67ec2a2ca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257250} :answer-field/id #uuid "c017c03d-1ac2-5b93-9628-5f5c0ad12c0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3df2ce8-a374-5f4f-80bf-b8dbf37e4ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-124694" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that  $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)={e}^{x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & ={e}^{x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =(t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =1+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}1+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & ={[t+{t}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[2+4-(1+1)] \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134212 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b6f0d80-4352-5158-8f93-1840b1e6324a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324725} {:answer/id #uuid "64abec96-fecf-52bf-b665-465ae20f4135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324804} {:answer/id #uuid "95deb8cb-eec5-56d6-b7c7-f205853e1f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325249} {:answer/id #uuid "9f9661da-4c00-5003-8d44-16815092e8eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{89}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325327} {:answer/id #uuid "b603e0fd-9b34-5f6e-b31b-3b2140f17ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{109}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b603e0fd-9b34-5f6e-b31b-3b2140f17ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{109}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325535} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3dfc2b-fd60-5b79-a0ca-b2bb5282bb22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326587}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7cef591-bf6c-502e-a297-4a0f671dac2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-39340" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)={x}^{2}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(x+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=3t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(2+t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=3t,\\,y=2+t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & ={x}^{2}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(x+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(3t)^{2}(2+t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =9{t}^{2}(2+t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(18{t}^{2}+9{t}^{3})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+t)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =((18{t}^{2}+9{t}^{3})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =54{t}^{2}+27{t}^{3}+3t+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}54{t}^{2}+27{t}^{3}+3t+1\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & ={[18{t}^{3}+\\frac{27}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(18+\\frac{27}{4}+\\frac{3}{2}+1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{109}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166e92fc-f76a-54b5-a0dd-63e74ebd5717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256986} {:answer/id #uuid "25c15736-d6ba-56e2-90f2-ba5a0588cc31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257104} {:answer/id #uuid "911d4916-bdd8-561f-b96d-1989bde4de80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258064} {:answer/id #uuid "d636aee9-1a04-5a63-b2bd-90b7b476ffb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258661} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c9c31a-af3d-5b26-a0c9-8f70bbe49d0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "911d4916-bdd8-561f-b96d-1989bde4de80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258064} :answer-field/id #uuid "3395a8a4-72d7-5431-a3bf-dbf9b39ab8be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259126}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ff38139-bd4b-55b1-a4ac-c9a0d7dde49f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124688" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that  $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(y-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(y-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\operatorname{cos}t-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}t)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =(\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\operatorname{cos}t-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t-\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t+\\operatorname{sin}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-(-1-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a1cc1e-6c7c-5eb5-8782-6185aaada67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257132} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5c1e37-56f1-50fb-b6d1-e94b31278780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257462} {:answer/id #uuid "6934487a-8eb1-5c6b-9b99-2f712e3ce1e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257716} {:answer/id #uuid "c098ca54-0767-55d1-a79d-5dd92229c601" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258464} {:answer/id #uuid "e724745c-f49d-514b-9248-b9b3caf11eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a1cc1e-6c7c-5eb5-8782-6185aaada67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257132} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e0b360f-7b50-508f-bc77-f1e69e16c0d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259059}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aaea8c36-ce4d-54ba-a2eb-6aed8473ac11" :question/math-academy-id "q-124689" :question/problem "Evaluate$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}t)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =(\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}t\\operatorname{cos}t-\\operatorname{sin}t(-\\operatorname{sin}t) \\\\  & ={\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =t\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\pi -0 \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259715 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "248ddbce-6070-5712-afac-3351be818687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257089} {:answer/id #uuid "650b1bbb-fae3-5145-829f-a04807f5d14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257669} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3dfb4b-820b-5b12-a401-88c1479f2704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258168} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e142f3-f380-597f-a2ec-0f4c63ea82f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258898} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbc0191-1988-5241-a6d2-3448d950e37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "650b1bbb-fae3-5145-829f-a04807f5d14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257669} :answer-field/id #uuid "c11f27a1-5eba-5c1b-9677-29d5ce54bfe4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259370}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18a06bdc-cb94-54a8-9fb9-6d1d6e3f27c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-124691" :question/problem "Evaluate  $$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=t\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}t)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}t+t\\operatorname{cos}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\operatorname{cos}t-t\\operatorname{sin}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =(t\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot ((\\operatorname{sin}t+t\\operatorname{cos}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\operatorname{cos}t-t\\operatorname{sin}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{sin}t(\\operatorname{sin}t+t\\operatorname{cos}t)+t\\operatorname{cos}t(\\operatorname{cos}t-t\\operatorname{sin}t) \\\\  & =t{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t+t{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t-{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t \\\\  & =t({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t) \\\\  & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{2}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =2{\\pi }^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aaf5016-f079-5a89-acf7-5d9a6c81a79e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257434} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad06c35-e2d5-5c92-9374-c0ee3dc71543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257435} {:answer/id #uuid "e008728e-7840-5a56-a663-2a5cf58d4b55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258734} {:answer/id #uuid "f192773f-28fe-5dff-8add-6f7c44d632d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258885} {:answer/id #uuid "f2eb3173-51d7-535e-aaa5-a8f0959fd452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ad06c35-e2d5-5c92-9374-c0ee3dc71543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257435} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5c9f6c2-e852-5e7b-bee8-30f1a7b46854" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259461}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b8d179c-8a3b-5f0a-ae95-7266bd00dc49" :question/math-academy-id "q-124693" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\,y={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =({t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & ={[{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[1-0] \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ad2868-cfa8-5e70-a096-102e472ce7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256798} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0343e0-516c-5453-92f1-46fc15399f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257439} {:answer/id #uuid "8e941010-5b37-5c05-b385-e2206c35e82c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258037} {:answer/id #uuid "a9298b81-fd3f-5dc0-9c39-af3414a2639f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258257} {:answer/id #uuid "a9acd370-6aed-5cc9-b5fe-f4f50c42aa0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01ad2868-cfa8-5e70-a096-102e472ce7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256798} :answer-field/id #uuid "573a9156-a300-5f27-97b1-a6a93a7b47a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259182}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5cfcca7d-9fbd-5623-b577-ba72ef3dd747" :question/math-academy-id "q-124696" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that $$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=\\frac{y+1}{x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}\n$$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)={t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(t-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [3,4].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y=t-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\frac{y+1}{x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{(t-1)+1}{{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{2({t}^{2}-1)}{t-1}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2(t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2(t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot 2t-2(t+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-2(t+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(-2t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & ={[-{t}^{2}]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =[-16+9] \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e9c9635-514f-5437-89a3-2311516df929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324616} {:answer/id #uuid "542f73e6-a0ee-5f63-a36b-e67fde3a6341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324669} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa4c2bd-e1e8-5ef1-b567-38d573db5658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324998} {:answer/id #uuid "98e23fb5-b473-5394-a5ba-4656c5c07d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325270} {:answer/id #uuid "9f5e0be4-5f46-5ddf-98a2-9f9d363b7d9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f5e0be4-5f46-5ddf-98a2-9f9d363b7d9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325323} :answer-field/id #uuid "526c7e14-1815-5fc1-a1ad-f65ad4c3be74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326361}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d6ca191-15db-5023-b8de-7e13937e634b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39422" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(y\\operatorname{sin}x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(x+y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path  $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\operatorname{arcsin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t,\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =2\\operatorname{sin}(\\operatorname{arcsin}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arcsin}t)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t) & =(2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r})\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =-2(\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}}-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37789fbf-187a-5931-87ee-f6efcb8d4882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567357} {:answer/id #uuid "406da1ca-1b0f-5a51-85fc-0d59b9f5c2b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567359} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb6d923-5c04-5b94-b393-aa363763c35c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567362} {:answer/id #uuid "84c3282d-d14b-5f40-af1f-205eaf8a9b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567369} {:answer/id #uuid "9a94a97f-e8ac-51dc-b17b-778c4e14f24b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37789fbf-187a-5931-87ee-f6efcb8d4882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567357} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dde938b-9bc6-56c2-8869-4846463cfa11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567367}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0809daf7-1c3a-50f9-b744-3b2f57eaa183" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x)\\,i+(- 2 y + 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\frac{\\pi}{2},2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- 2 x)\\,i+(- 2 y + 2)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- 2 \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j \\\\  & =(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left((- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left((3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 18 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(18 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left[6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\\\  & =((6))-((0)) \\\\  & =(6)-(0) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067d7587-bd7a-55ca-b2a9-817044886453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567349} {:answer/id #uuid "33f9719e-3e95-52b4-919a-e855b575c1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567355} {:answer/id #uuid "5d9eb42f-0bfc-567b-a6cf-e1098750c4ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567363} {:answer/id #uuid "9147b4dd-04fe-5fd1-8299-b6061cdd5d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567373} {:answer/id #uuid "b5966bc5-1c82-5adb-b53d-5dcb7e743f51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f9719e-3e95-52b4-919a-e855b575c1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567355} :answer-field/id #uuid "632e0419-a120-5f91-b9be-603360314bbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567364}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "337254b1-2fa0-54a0-9d70-76189ce2de0c" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(x^{2} y)\\,i+(x + 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(2 t)\\,i+(t + 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2 t,\\quad y=t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(x^{2} y)\\,i+(x + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(2 t\\right)^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\left(2 t\\right) + 1\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(4 t^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right))\\,i+(2 t + 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(2)\\,i+(1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\left((4 t^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right))\\,i+(2 t + 1)\\,j\\right)\\cdot\\left((2)\\,i+(1)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &=(4 t^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right))\\cdot(2)+(2 t + 1)\\cdot(1) \\\\ &=(8 t^{3} + 8 t^{2})+(2 t + 1) \\\\ &=8 t^{3} + 8 t^{2} + 2 t + 1\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}(8 t^{3} + 8 t^{2} + 2 t + 1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[2 t^{4} + \\frac{8 t^{3}}{3} + t^{2} + t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((1)+(1)+(2)+\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right))-((0)+(0)+(0)+(0)) \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{20}{3}\\right)-(0) \\\\ &=\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f959b2-0ffe-576b-9e02-b7396da8770a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30 - \\frac{15 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567351} {:answer/id #uuid "76ba4b8e-08a9-5d7d-acec-c1ba3fa23731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567366} {:answer/id #uuid "8758f828-2dc9-5477-aa58-2e3270158b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567370} {:answer/id #uuid "c75678bd-5ef0-563a-a7a9-134f15b2947f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567377} {:answer/id #uuid "d941523f-47c5-5e3a-8409-70777fef6ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d941523f-47c5-5e3a-8409-70777fef6ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567380} :answer-field/id #uuid "9820ad9d-0462-5026-b84e-b4ae332e6b83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567374}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "360cbd2a-7568-5a87-84ac-a04c5046eb33" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(5 x)\\,i+(5 y - 5)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\frac{\\pi}{2},2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(5 x)\\,i+(5 y - 5)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(5 \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(5 \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 5\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 5)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j \\\\  & =(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left((15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 5)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left((3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 5) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(45 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(- 45 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}(15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left[- 15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\\\  & =((-15))-((0)) \\\\  & =(-15)-(0) \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c6c388f-6945-5085-a52f-1550351c42c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-7\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567353} {:answer/id #uuid "8e57943f-170c-50e6-b5b2-adf2146e2c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(9\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567372} {:answer/id #uuid "cc47fc32-7150-505d-bbc7-14230ad6a69f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567378} {:answer/id #uuid "d20656cd-722a-5245-b740-acf463570a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567379} {:answer/id #uuid "f78fa774-904e-5be7-a83f-6cd598799e95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-11\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c6c388f-6945-5085-a52f-1550351c42c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-7\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567353} :answer-field/id #uuid "16fa1355-c929-5c19-8a01-ccbc29477515" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567352}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "759e78d6-7a3c-53d5-83ac-8b0533a5e4b8" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=(-5)\\left(\\frac{y+1}{x}\\,i-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\,j\\right)\n$$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [3,4].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y=t-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(-5)\\left(\\frac{y+1}{x}\\,i-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\,j\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left(\\frac{(t-1)+1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{2({t}^{2}-1)}{t-1}\\,j\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-2(t+1)\\,j\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(-5)\\left((\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-2(t+1)\\,j)\\right)\\cdot (2t\\,i+j) \\\\ &=(-5)\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot 2t-2(t+1)\\cdot 1\\right) \\\\ &=(-5)\\left(2-2(t+1)\\cdot 1\\right) \\\\ &=(-5)\\left(-2t\\right).\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-5)\\left({\\int }_{3}^{4}(-2t)\\,dt\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left({[-{t}^{2}]}_{3}^{4}\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left([-16+9]\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left(-7\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dc4ce1e-eafd-5783-9383-568f1601d09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(-4-\\sqrt{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567358} {:answer/id #uuid "4bec57b6-4b6a-5921-a981-9e3f449068b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(-2+\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567361} {:answer/id #uuid "8a03e0c2-20dc-5c9e-aa85-b421c94b43e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(\\sqrt{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567371} {:answer/id #uuid "de8a8253-5270-5081-8567-22d741f3d493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(1-\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567381} {:answer/id #uuid "f955c89d-840b-5d78-8735-84aef633daff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(2-\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f955c89d-840b-5d78-8735-84aef633daff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(2-\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567383} :answer-field/id #uuid "4702667f-3b1e-5bd1-81e7-1a8c1903dba7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567360}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "825d8f89-9569-5641-b2e2-7d7b47441607" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(-1)\\left((y\\operatorname{\\sin}x)\\,i+(x+y)\\,j\\right)$ and $C$ is the path  $r(t)=\\operatorname{arcsin}t\\,i+2j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}t,\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(-1)\\left(2\\operatorname{\\sin}(\\operatorname{arcsin}t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &=(-1)\\left(2t\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\,j\\right).\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arcsin}t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(-1)\\left((2t\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\,j)\\right)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i) \\\\ &=(-1)\\left(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\right).\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-1)\\left({\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,dt\\right) \\\\  & =(-1)\\left(-2\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2}\\right) \\\\  & =(-1)\\left(-2(\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}}-1)\\right) \\\\  & =(-1)\\left(2-\\sqrt{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8bbc97-aee7-51d5-a133-62f51f9489d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711714} {:answer/id #uuid "3731eb81-c2ef-5ad6-8c65-18e7386f58ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711717} {:answer/id #uuid "5169f893-6e2b-579b-9c00-cfc40967b1fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac\\pi2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711718} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbca83f-456b-524a-b6bd-7ac92a6c8a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711722} {:answer/id #uuid "b26dae46-00d3-5e40-a78d-ff640f8328e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3731eb81-c2ef-5ad6-8c65-18e7386f58ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711717} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee710f8-ba9c-5dc4-9bd9-a4334891732a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711712}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1129c3c2-8035-555f-8741-73e78e4cc223" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf i-x\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf r(t)=\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\le t\\le\\frac\\pi2$." :question/worked-solution "Use\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\nAlong the path, $x=\\sin t$ and $y=\\cos t$, so\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))=\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nDifferentiate the supplied path:\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nThen\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=\\cos^2t+(-\\sin t)(-\\sin t)\\\\\n&=\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}1\\,\\mathrm dt\n=\\left[t\\right]_0^{\\pi/2}=\\frac\\pi2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371f8358-fa99-5be1-81d4-9c3a0e9c4d5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711716} {:answer/id #uuid "6c82d25c-21a7-52f1-b9c3-a44aa4beea0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711720} {:answer/id #uuid "b60d756f-615f-5961-adf0-4c8382195801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^2+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711725} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ea4fbe-47ad-512f-b024-a377a71dd1f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711727} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e02e42-f612-53fd-99f4-1d78a5ae32c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371f8358-fa99-5be1-81d4-9c3a0e9c4d5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711716} :answer-field/id #uuid "754efe93-295b-561d-8662-bcad696fd3bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6bf0d7bf-cb75-5497-944d-ce9561ee4d19" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y)=x\\,\\mathbf i+(y-1)\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf r(t)=t\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+t\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\le t\\le\\pi$." :question/worked-solution "Use the parametrized line-integral formula:\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^\\pi\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\nSubstitute $x=t\\sin t$ and $y=t\\cos t$:\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\n=t\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+(t\\cos t-1)\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nBoth coordinates require the product rule:\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\,\\mathbf i\n+(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nTake the dot product and expand:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=t\\sin t(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\\\\n&\\quad +(t\\cos t-1)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\\\\n&=t\\sin^2t+t^2\\sin t\\cos t\\\\\n&\\quad +t\\cos^2t-t^2\\sin t\\cos t\\\\\n&\\quad -\\cos t+t\\sin t\\\\\n&=t-\\cos t+t\\sin t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe mixed terms cancel, but the offset in the field leaves two extra terms. To integrate them, note that\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(-t\\cos t)=-\\cos t+t\\sin t.\n$$\nThus\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n&=\\int_0^\\pi(t-\\cos t+t\\sin t)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{t^2}{2}-t\\cos t\\right]_0^\\pi\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-\\pi(-1)-0\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}+\\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c6f668c-17e0-550c-bf01-07a12e658a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711711} {:answer/id #uuid "242cea8a-d0d6-5ff9-9db9-609f69774db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711715} {:answer/id #uuid "a2bb4c6b-fa10-5de9-b170-dacdd38a93fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711723} {:answer/id #uuid "b899e334-7875-55b2-b64e-9bf5bc3fd58a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711726} {:answer/id #uuid "e56381ff-011f-5196-bb9e-db008932bf3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2bb4c6b-fa10-5de9-b170-dacdd38a93fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711723} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcec324f-3af8-569f-b853-9e9716a7a80e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711729}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea656ca1-5eae-5f73-9742-a04c3fb0299d" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf i+(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is given by $\\mathbf r(t)=(1+2t)\\,\\mathbf i+(2-t)\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\le t\\le1$.\n\n*Hint: Use*\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^1\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt,\n\\qquad \\mathbf r'(t)=2\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Along the path, $x=1+2t$ and $y=2-t$. Substitute both coordinates into the field:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\n&=(2-t)\\,\\mathbf i+((1+2t)+(2-t))\\,\\mathbf j\\\\\n&=(2-t)\\,\\mathbf i+(3+t)\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nDifferentiating the path gives $\\mathbf r'(t)=2\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j$. Take the dot product, keeping the negative sign of the second tangent component:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=2(2-t)-(3+t)\\\\\n&=1-3t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nNow evaluate the definite integral:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n&=\\int_0^1(1-3t)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[t-\\frac32t^2\\right]_0^1\\\\\n&=1-\\frac32=-\\frac12.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30173ae3-8e67-51ee-8f89-6d95e51d48f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712371} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8af6c3-3974-551e-86c5-54fae030a860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712375} {:answer/id #uuid "6a176c1e-75bb-5e7b-9fc7-a3eff06746aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712379} {:answer/id #uuid "786bf17a-0e1a-5dcd-9358-c27d37d5dae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712382} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ebf3b9-f2c5-5fbf-a6bb-dcc503a0fa0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "786bf17a-0e1a-5dcd-9358-c27d37d5dae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712382} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77e2fca-86f8-5a8b-908f-6953377a408c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712391}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d7a881e-8d60-5bd0-b8bc-99254fd65d35" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 y - 1)\\,i+(2 x - y + 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(- 2 t - 2)\\,i+(- t - 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n$$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 2,\\quad y=- t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(2 y - 1)\\,i+(2 x - y + 1)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 \\left(- t - 1\\right) - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(2 \\left(- 2 t - 2\\right) - \\left(- t - 1\\right) + 1\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 2 t - 3)\\,i+(- 3 t - 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t - 2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(-2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 2 t - 3)\\,i+(- 3 t - 2)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(-2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t - 3)\\cdot(-2)+(- 3 t - 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(-1)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\left({4 t + 6}\\right)+\\left({3 t + 2}\\right) \\\\ &=7 t + 8\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({7 t + 8}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{\\frac{7 t^{2}}{2} + 8 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((8)+\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{23}{2}\\right)-(0) \\\\ &=\\frac{23}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17632d48-0b54-592e-a841-a1a207465cb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712369} {:answer/id #uuid "7318685a-323a-5513-ac96-3dcba61f2139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712380} {:answer/id #uuid "b53a9d1c-a494-508d-9584-dc064df6b7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712389} {:answer/id #uuid "b624ba7b-71a9-5226-9d1b-280c84468974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712390} {:answer/id #uuid "ba485208-6ed9-5a36-bcce-ecad72f4b48c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b53a9d1c-a494-508d-9584-dc064df6b7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712389} :answer-field/id #uuid "76e64c52-0983-57fd-93c6-b5342a5a7984" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712381}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43aa9df2-3303-53b3-a49e-7ba0e92cb9e8" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- y)\\,i+(- x - 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t + 2)\\,i+(2 t + 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n$$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t + 2,\\quad y=2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- y)\\,i+(- x - 2)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- \\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(- \\left(t + 2\\right) - 2\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 2 t - 1)\\,i+(- t - 4)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t + 2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 2 t - 1)\\,i+(- t - 4)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 2 t - 1)\\cdot(1)+(- t - 4)\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 2 t - 1}\\right)+\\left({- 2 t - 8}\\right) \\\\ &=- 4 t - 9\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 4 t - 9}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- 2 t^{2} - 9 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-9)+(-2))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(-11)-(0) \\\\ &=-11\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "438852ab-3dd5-582b-aa84-759aaf3b786a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712373} {:answer/id #uuid "56f069f9-f6b5-54de-bd9f-0b5958dfbe71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712376} {:answer/id #uuid "8545e4a7-9b79-5fe1-9107-f407f1642d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712383} {:answer/id #uuid "bb261588-6384-5511-bb1c-25d550c083b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712394} {:answer/id #uuid "e408771b-bca0-56fa-ab5d-3c55ecaa9934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e408771b-bca0-56fa-ab5d-3c55ecaa9934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712399} :answer-field/id #uuid "869b80d6-b62c-5baa-a9c9-6ecb7efd3eff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712384}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c3aca75-294e-5fea-b965-6baeaac7a8b2" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 y)\\,i+(- 2 x)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t - 2)\\,i+(2 t + 2)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n$$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t - 2,\\quad y=2 t + 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- 2 y)\\,i+(- 2 x)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- 2 \\left(2 t + 2\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 \\left(t - 2\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 4 t - 4)\\,i+(- 2 t + 4)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 2)\\,j \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 4 t - 4)\\,i+(- 2 t + 4)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 t - 4)\\cdot(1)+(- 2 t + 4)\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 4 t - 4}\\right)+\\left({- 4 t + 8}\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t + 4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 8 t + 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- 4 t^{2} + 4 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-4)+(4))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(0)-(0) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae63b8e-ae9a-5bb2-90e4-144b06291077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712370} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0dbb0f-eeef-595d-8c3e-69a77725ee44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712372} {:answer/id #uuid "5b80454d-bf9f-534a-b9a4-fc57252dcaae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712377} {:answer/id #uuid "932fb550-b045-5de4-b81e-757813772386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712386} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e4b6a7-5b71-557b-b85c-170100c69e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "932fb550-b045-5de4-b81e-757813772386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712386} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba9bf6c8-2c06-5140-955b-faffabc9c80c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712393}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f8c8036-de79-5449-a62b-4bda22066e3c" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- y + 1)\\,i+(- x + 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(- t)\\,i+(- t - 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n$$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- t,\\quad y=- t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- y + 1)\\,i+(- x + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- \\left(- t - 1\\right) + 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(- \\left(- t\\right) + 1\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(t + 2)\\,i+(t + 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(-1)\\,i+(-1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(t + 2)\\,i+(t + 1)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(-1)\\,i+(-1)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(t + 2)\\cdot(-1)+(t + 1)\\cdot(-1) \\\\ &=\\left({- t - 2}\\right)+\\left({- t - 1}\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 t - 3\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 2 t - 3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- t^{2} - 3 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-1)+(-3))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(-4)-(0) \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712400 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13e447b5-faca-5a5f-9083-9792edef2df5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712368} {:answer/id #uuid "8e39e322-43d4-5827-912a-972febce881b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712385} {:answer/id #uuid "a7554cc5-3148-54d7-8545-a60ecc25d725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712388} {:answer/id #uuid "d5219b2e-d7d5-540a-bc1e-6c6401c12803" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712397} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7c5ab3-2069-56a6-b689-4f5982f840ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13e447b5-faca-5a5f-9083-9792edef2df5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712368} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb789be4-5b0f-5cca-83ca-dfe527339637" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712395}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8a56c7d-30ab-5d35-b00b-bf5e54fe584e" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 y + 2)\\,i+(- 2 x - 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t - 1)\\,i+(2 t - 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n$$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t - 1,\\quad y=2 t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- 2 y + 2)\\,i+(- 2 x - 2)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- 2 \\left(2 t - 1\\right) + 2\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(- 2 \\left(t - 1\\right) - 2\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 t + 4)\\,i+(- 2 t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 4 t + 4)\\,i+(- 2 t)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 t + 4)\\cdot(1)+(- 2 t)\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 4 t + 4}\\right)+\\left({- 4 t}\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t + 4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 8 t + 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- 4 t^{2} + 4 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-4)+(4))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(0)-(0) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f882330-5fa5-55e2-95d1-7e79678dc6eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712443} {:answer/id #uuid "5c534942-8fa9-52b6-a60c-efd5b29e0848" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712449} {:answer/id #uuid "6e88684d-7b8d-5a90-8507-7fa6ed89917b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712450} {:answer/id #uuid "8aeb8921-8724-5198-978a-d76050baa356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712454} {:answer/id #uuid "970dacda-86cd-59dc-9dec-a98958efb7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 4 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c534942-8fa9-52b6-a60c-efd5b29e0848" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712449} :answer-field/id #uuid "9daf3be8-f67e-5de9-b5c9-f956b9ba588a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "483e4ae6-79d4-5247-8e94-b6fc63ccde3d" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x + 1)\\,i+(- 2 y - 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- 2 x + 1)\\,i+(- 2 y - 1)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 1\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\left({\\begin{aligned}&t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- t^{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((- 4 \\pi^{2})+(0)+(- 2 \\pi)) \\\\ &{} -((0)+(0)+(0))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 \\pi^{2} - 2 \\pi)-(0) \\\\ &=- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(- t^{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d48242b-6023-5db7-8d3a-eeecb6026126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\left(4 + 5 \\pi\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712442} {:answer/id #uuid "6e88f163-54a1-5d50-9758-c76af130019a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712451} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bb970f-214a-5e0c-9e0d-2f2a0c88e94d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712461} {:answer/id #uuid "e2037cf7-ebea-5360-9d1d-cb3ea7e9f088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712464} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f9a9b7-eb83-56cd-b7b6-22fbbf7aac3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\left(- 5 \\pi - 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e88f163-54a1-5d50-9758-c76af130019a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712451} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cce83b1-f5e4-552f-8181-ec9a1b346cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712439}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "83d3c56a-8bde-57d4-8339-cfbeec8ae536" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(x + 1)\\,i+(y + 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\pi,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(x + 1)\\,i+(y + 2)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(\\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{\\frac{t^{2}}{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((2 \\pi^{2})+(0)+(4 \\pi)) \\\\ &{} -(\\left(\\frac{\\pi^{2}}{2}\\right)+(0)+(- 2 \\pi))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(4 \\pi + 2 \\pi^{2})-(- 2 \\pi + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{2}) \\\\ &=\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712463 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21c60d00-9b09-5422-ad29-73cb2388f6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712441} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbc11ad-ba0e-50f4-a146-480e3f613902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712444} {:answer/id #uuid "51619b82-99ba-5533-81dd-94de10a3c468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\pi - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712448} {:answer/id #uuid "7df4856f-c431-5056-9b88-a9efa4468f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712452} {:answer/id #uuid "c295ba11-ac49-5b1e-b3b1-caab94b667cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21c60d00-9b09-5422-ad29-73cb2388f6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712441} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ef5e5c7-f47c-50f1-a460-e32ac79f1ac9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "de586386-7b1f-5d2e-a48c-3a3bc19f3b4f" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 x - 1)\\,i+(2 y - 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\pi,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(2 x - 1)\\,i+(2 y - 2)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 \\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(2 \\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 2\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + 2 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{t^{2} - t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((4 \\pi^{2})+(0)+(- 4 \\pi)) \\\\ &{} -((\\pi^{2})+(0)+(2 \\pi))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 \\pi + 4 \\pi^{2})-(2 \\pi + \\pi^{2}) \\\\ &=3 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(t^{2} - t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d34f86b-71a3-5f3b-a87d-b499775f5feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\pi^{2} - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712440} {:answer/id #uuid "514f41cd-6266-5f8a-9dc4-f9ffe2f6fa3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712447} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e83f54-e849-594d-8929-7f7b5b427aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712458} {:answer/id #uuid "c5675a16-3166-526a-be47-5e167558bd95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712460} {:answer/id #uuid "da681b53-3a27-5749-ab3b-8bf3dcad2440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9e83f54-e849-594d-8929-7f7b5b427aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712458} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb08b1c-a405-5c9d-aafd-4b0c7581df71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712457}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ec707abf-6267-5e8a-ab61-e05c91f03ed9" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x + 2)\\,i+(- 2 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\pi,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- 2 x + 2)\\,i+(- 2 y)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left({2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- t^{2} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=((- 4 \\pi^{2})+(0))-((- \\pi^{2})+(0)) \\\\ &=(- 4 \\pi^{2})-(- \\pi^{2}) \\\\ &=- 3 \\pi^{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(- t^{2} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Line Integrals of a Vector-Valued Functions Over Plane Curves"}]}
